     CDS             428147..428617
                     /gene="rpsG"
                     /locus_tag="ABO_0381"
                     /function="One of the primary rRNA binding proteins, it
                     binds directly to 16S rRNA where it nucleates assembly of
                     the head domain of the 30S subunit. Is located at the
                     subunit interface close to the decoding center, where it
                     has been shown to contact mRNA. Probably blocks exit of
                     the e-site tRNA (by similarity). Protein S7 is also a
                     translational repressor protein; it regulates the
                     expression of the str operon members to different degrees
                     by binding to its mRNA."
                     /note="binds directly to 16S rRNA where it nucleates
                     assembly of the head domain of the 30S subunit"
