                     /db_xref="GeneID:4212374"
     CDS             460074..460706
                     /gene="rpsD"
                     /locus_tag="ABO_0421"
                     /function="One of two assembly initiator proteins for the
                     30S subunit, it binds directly to 16S rRNA where it
                     nucleates assembly of the body of the 30S subunit. With S5
                     and S12 plays an important role in translational accuracy;
                     many suppressors of streptomycin-dependent mutants of
                     protein S12 are found in this protein, some but not all of
                     which decrease translational accuracy (ram, ribosomal
                     ambiguity mutations)."
                     /function="Protein S4 is also a translational repressor
                     protein, it controls the translation of the alpha-operon
                     (which codes for S13, S11, S4, RNA polymerase alpha
                     subunit, and L17) by binding to its mRNA. Also functions
                     as a rho-dependent antiterminator of rRNA transcription,
                     increasing the synthesis of rRNA under conditions of
                     excess protein, allowing a more rapid return to
                     homeostasis. Binds directly to RNA polymerase."
                     /note="(ribosomal protein S4) identified by sequence
                     similarity; InterPro: Ribosomal protein S4;
                     High confidence in function and specificity"
                     /codon_start=1
                     /transl_table=11
                     /product="30S ribosomal protein S4"
