                     /EC_number="2.1.1.31"
                     /function="is one of several nucleases operating together
                     with the tRNA-modifying enzymes before the formation of
                     the mature tRNA. It catalyses the
                     reaction:S-adenosyl-L-methionine + tRNA ->
                     S-adenosyl-L-homocysteine + tRNA
                     containingN1-methylguanine, methylating guanosine(G) to
                     N1-methylguanine (1-methylguanosine (m1G)) at position 37
                     of tRNAs that read CUN (leucine), CCN(proline), and CGG
                     (arginine) codons. The presence of m1G improves the
                     cellular growth rate and the polypeptide steptime and also
                     prevents the tRNA from shifting the reading frame"
                     /note="identified by sequence similarity; InterPro: tRNA
                     (guanine-N1-)-methyltransferase;
