     CDS             1275901..1276239
                     /gene="glnK-1"
                     /locus_tag="ABO_1123"
                     /function="P-II indirectly controls the transcription of
                     the glutamine synthetase gene (glnA). P-II prevents nr-ii
                     catalyzed conversion of nr-i to nr-i-phosphate, the
                     transcriptional activator of glnA. when P-II is
                     uridylylated to P-II-UMP, these events are reversed. when
                     the ratio of gln to 2-ketoglutarate decreases, P-II is
                     uridylylated to P-II-UMP, which causes the deadenylylation
                     of glutamine synthetase by glnE, so activating the
                     enzyme."
