                     /gene="rnhA"
                     /locus_tag="ABO_1224"
                     /EC_number="3.1.26.4"
                     /function="This enzyme is an endonuclease that degrades
                     the RNA of RNA-DNA hybrids specifically. In E.coli RNAse H
                     participates in DNA replication; it helps to specify the
                     origin of genomic replication by suppressing initiation at
                     origins other than the locus oric; along with the 5'-3'
                     exonuclease of pol1, it removes RNA primers from the
                     Okazaki fragments of lagging strand synthesis."
