     CDS             complement(1451402..1451869)
                     /locus_tag="ABO_1276"
                     /function="responsible for removing an oxidatively damaged
                     form of guanine (8-hydroxy- guanine or
                     7,8-dihydro-8-oxoguanine) from DNA and the nucleotide
                     pool. 8-oxo-dGTP is inserted opposite dA and dC residues
                     of template DNA with near equal efficiency, leading to A.T
                     to G.C transversions. MutT specifically degrades
                     8-oxo-dGTP to the monophosphate, with the concomitant
                     release of pyrophosphate."
