                     /EC_number="4.2.99.18"
                     /function="Has both an apurinic and/or apyrimidinic
                     endonuclease activity and a DNA n-glycosylase activity.
                     Incises damaged DNA at cytosines, thymines and guanines.
                     Acts on a damaged strand, 5' from the damaged site.
                     Required for the repair of both oxidative DNA damage and
                     spontaneous mutagenic lesions. Catalytic activity: the
                     c-o-p bond 3' to the apurinic or apyrimidinic site in DNA
                     is broken by a beta-elimination reaction, leaving a
                     3'-terminal unsaturated sugar and a product with a
                     terminal 5'-phosphate."
